        "score": 4,
        "rationale": "The single-job e2e wiring as described (caller-side if: failure()/if: success(), post+resolve pair, one marker, log path from the tee) matches the convention, but the multi-job visual-regression workflow was wired as per-job bare failure()/success() steps inside chromium and firefox instead of the documented final needs: job with if: always()/!cancelled() gating on needs.<job>.result, and with two markers in one workflow rather than one per workflow; no job.status or in-action gating is evident, but the empty diff and vanished worktree mean none of this can be verified against actual files."
      },
